pySMESH: Cartesian_3D with viscous layers keeps every cut cell of its offset mesh that has
volume, so the layers have no void (SMESH V9_16_0; applies after
StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_viscous_submeshes.patch).

Defect: a mesh from Cartesian_3D with viscous layers can have voids in the layer region, and
the compute reports success.

Symptom: a cylinder of radius 1 and height 2, layers on every face (0.2 thick, 3 layers,
factor 1.2), grid spacing 0.25: 192 layer cells have a facet on the mesh boundary that no face
covers, 48 boundary faces lie inside the mesh at radius 0.78, and the layer volume is 2.846
against 3.002 for a mesh with no void. A hexagonal prism at spacing 0.1 misses 3.3 % of its
volume. With size_threshold 1000 in CartesianParameters3D both are complete.

Root cause, measured: the inner compute meshes the offset shape and drops each cut cell
smaller than 1/size_threshold of a full cell (Hexahedron::checkPolyhedronSize,
StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_Hexahedron.cxx:3192; the default threshold is 4). A dropped cell
leaves a dent in the offset boundary. The faces around the dent do not lie on an offset FACE,
so they go to the SOLID (:4224-4251). MakeViscousLayers grows layers only from the faces of
the offset FACEs (makePrisms), so no layer grows over a dent, and the dent faces stay inside
the copied mesh.

Change, in StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx only: in the inner compute of the viscous path, the
grid's size threshold is infinite, so only a cut cell with no volume is dropped. The offset
boundary then lies on the offset FACEs everywhere.

Not changed: the plain path, which still applies size_threshold.
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
@@ -213,6 +213,10 @@
     {
       grid._toAddEdges = true;
       grid._toCreateFaces = true;
+      // pySMESH: the layers grow from the boundary faces of the offset FACEs. A cut cell
+      // dropped as too small leaves a dent whose faces go to the SOLID, so no layer grows
+      // there and the mesh has a void. Drop only a cell with no volume.
+      grid._sizeThreshold = std::numeric_limits< double >::infinity();
     }
 
     const auto numOfThreads = std::thread::hardware_concurrency() == 0 ? 1 : std::thread::hardware_concurrency();
